<TextPage
  title="Disclosure — SproutChores"
  description="Our honest disclosure policy. SproutChores currently runs no ads and no affiliate links; if that ever changes, this page tells you exactly how and where."
  h1="Disclosure"
>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 8 June 2026</p>

  <h2>Right now</h2>
  <p>
    SproutChores currently displays <strong>no advertising</strong> and contains <strong>no affiliate
    links</strong>. Everything here is free, and we make no money from the tools or articles today.
  </p>

  <h2>If that changes</h2>
  <p>
    To keep the site free, we may add advertising or affiliate links in the future. If we do, we'll be
    transparent about it:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Affiliate links:</strong> some links may earn us a small commission if you buy through
      them, at no extra cost to you. Where affiliate links appear, we'll label them clearly. We only
      ever recommend things we'd genuinely suggest to another parent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Amazon Associates:</strong> if we join the program, the following applies — "As an
      Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases." Any such links will be disclosed on the
      pages where they appear.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Advertising:</strong> if we run display ads, they'll be clearly distinguishable from our
      content, and our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> will be updated to explain any related
      data use and consent.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our promise</h2>
  <p>
    Recommendations will always be based on what we actually believe helps families — never on what
    pays the most. Money will never change the advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:hello@sproutchores.com">hello@sproutchores.com</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
